{
  "case_id": "2020-19-351",
  "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:24 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jonathan M. Freiman",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When Congress enacted the expropriation exception in 1976, Communist states had been engaging in widespread expropriation of property from American nationals and denying that the international law of takings required them to pay compensation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jonathan M. Freiman",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0000-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress can take these risks if it wants to, but it hasn't yet."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can that be a part of genocide? Can that taking be a part of genocide, not separate from genocide?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jonathan M. Freiman",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, Your Honor, if, in fact, a -- a country is taking property with the intent of physically destroying a people or a part of a people, it -- it's unquestionably a genocidal act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And to follow up on questions asked by Justices Sotomayor and Kagan, why isn't that the end of the case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Freiman",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This Court held in Samantar that the mere fact that something is literally possible does not mean it's what -- it's what the text meant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Would it still raise the concerns implicated by a very, very large judgment against a foreign country?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Freiman",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'd like to, I guess, raise three reasons for skepticism about the broad reading of (a)(3) that plaintiffs provide, and the first two track what you heard earlier of Simon."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0001-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The United States deplores the atrocities committed against victims of the Nazi regime and has long had a policy of encouraging Germany and other countries to provide mechanisms to afford a measure of justice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well, international law at the time recognized the international crime of genocide, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Good morning, Mr. Kneedler. I -- I understand your argument that the Clarification Act only works to address limits on the commercial activity requirement. But (h)(2) does exempt Nazi-era claims, and -- where the action is \"based on a claim that such work was taken in connection with the acts of a foreign government as part of a systematic campaign of coercive confiscation or misappropriation of works from members of a targeted and vulnerable group.\" Doesn't that seem to anticipate that there will be such claims that can be brought under (a)(3)?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So what, in your view, is the justification for denying compensation to citizens of the country in question or, maybe stated the other way, what harms would result from recognizing claims that outweigh the benefits of recognizing the claims?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0002-0021",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But corresponding to that, this Court has often said, in Sabbatino and elsewhere, that the -- that that principle is limited to the taking of property of aliens because, as a general principle, the treatment of a country of -- of its own nationals is not a matter of international concern."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BARRETT",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Kneedler, I have a question about what the Clarification Act should tell us about the expropriation exception."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0002-0022",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, in showing special solicitude for Nazi-era claims, the Clarification Act clearly assumes that some such claims against Nazi-era confiscations of property would be going forward and that the Foreign Sovereign Immunities Act would not bar them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0002-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, really, what Congress was doing was not taking away the opportunity of someone who had such a claim to rely on the loan of property to a U.S. museum as establishing the commercial nexus, but it didn't do more than that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0002-0011",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Foreign Sovereign Immunities Act provides jurisdiction over cases in which rights and property taken in violation of international law are at issue. The ordinary and natural meaning of that phrase, chosen by Congress, applies to Petitioners' property takings during the Holocaust."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0002-0014",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The first is the claim that the international human rights norm has to sound in the taking of property in the first instance and that those other norms do not."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice THOMAS",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "understand how it would make a difference to have one sequence versus the other, that you commit the genocide before you take the property or the property before you take the -- the -- before you commit the genocide."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0002-0020",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Because the violation of the international norm, Your Honor, doesn't cause the deprivation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I want to make sure I understand the scope of your argument. At times in your brief, particularly when you refer to the absence from the provision in question of any reference to aliens, you seem to be making an argument that would apply to any domestic taking. But that's not your argument, am I right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Okay. So is -- is it your argument that any taking that violates any principle of international law would be covered, or is your argument limited to those acts that constitute genocide or those that are part of a campaign of genocide, or is it a Holocaust-specific argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. O'Donnell)",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "My argument, Your Honor, is it -- it -- it extends certainly to genocide, it extends certainly to the Holocaust, and it would extend to other norms of which I can't think of any, where, as I said to Justice Breyer, it is a -- it is a violation of the norm itself that causes the property taking."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Even if it's limited to genocide -- there have been many incidents in the past that some people claim are genocidal. Sometimes these are hotly disputed. I won't go through the list. I hope there won't be more in the future, but, given human nature, that's a possibility. Wouldn't your argument require courts to decide whether a particular event that indisputably involved atrocities amounted to genocide?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. O'Donnell, Judge Katsas in one of his dissents made the point that your position would create a kind of strange dichotomy whereby victims of the Holocaust could bring suit for property deprivations, but their relatives or -- or -- you know, could not bring suit for their deaths. So why would that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And that's because \"taking\" is a term of art and \"taken\" is not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. O'Donnell)",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 76,
        "start": 76
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yes, Your Honor. And I actually think that the Court's guidance in OBB is instructive on this, right? The commercial activity exception asks if the claim arises out of commercial activity in the United States, and the Court was very clear that that doesn't mean but for. That doesn't mean alongside of which, right? The plaintiff in that case wouldn't have been injured in Austria if he or she hadn't bought the ticket in the United States, but that wasn't enough."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 78,
        "start": 78
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Good afternoon, Mr. O'Donnell. I'm interested in whether you could have brought this suit in any country other than Germany? In other words, does any other country waive sovereign immunity for foreign nations' domestic takings?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. O'Donnell)",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0003-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 78,
        "start": 78
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I am aware of none."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0004-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 85,
        "start": 85
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioners' argument boils down to this, that despite the absence of language in the FSIA as originally passed that would limit claims based on the nationality of victims of government property takings and despite the presence in the Clarification Act of language specifically recognizing the full extent of the Nazi regime's art looting and forced sales as properly within the expropriation exception, that unique among Nazi victims, Congress intended to disadvantage the Nazi's first victims, German Jews. This makes no sense."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Freiman",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0004-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Second of all, with regard to what to do if you find that the expropriation exception applies only to violations of the international law of takings, this is not a situation where remand is appropriate."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-351",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-357e8872f659-0004-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 90,
        "start": 90
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "counsel. The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 12:52 p.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
    {
